{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/118911-attachment-of-touchstones","id":118911,"title":"Attachment of Touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-24T20:50:00-07:00","id":118911,"title":"Attachment of Touchstones","content":"Just for clarification, if a Touchstone becomes detached due to Humanity loss, can it be re-attached just by regaining the appropriate Humanity level, or must the Touchstone Merit be purchased as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T21:01:53-07:00","id":118916,"title":"","content":"You do not have to buy the Touchstone merit to regain a detached touchstone. In fact, there's no way you could reattach a touchstone with the Merit, since each dot of the Merit gives you a new touchstone attached to the next lowest Humanity. HOWEVER, you also don't automatically regain a detached touchstone when you buy your Humanity back up. Remember, the Touchstone represents a relationship, and detachment represents that bridge being burned. You can certainly rebuild that connection over time, but it takes a significant effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T00:42:41-07:00","id":118985,"title":"","content":"Umm.. Actually, Touchstones are not lost when you lose your humanity. Detached touchstone no longer protects your humanity (by giving bonus dice to detachment rolls), however it is still your touchstone, you can gain willpower from it. Also if you LOSE all your touchstones, you're at a -3 dice penalty to your detachments, while if you have all your touchstones DETACHED you don't get any bonus nor penalty to your detachment rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:02:15-07:00","id":119067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/118911-attachment-of-touchstones?p=118985#post118985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm.. Actually, Touchstones are not lost when you lose your humanity. Detached touchstone no longer protects your humanity (by giving bonus dice to detachment rolls), however it is still your touchstone, you can gain willpower from it. Also if you LOSE all your touchstones, you're at a -3 dice penalty to your detachments, while if you have all your touchstones DETACHED you don't get any bonus nor penalty to your detachment rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, that's why I used the word detached and not the word lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:10:30-07:00","id":119070,"title":"","content":"And you're wrong. A touchstone becomes detached once your humanity drops. That can happens for a million reason that are completely unrelated to the touchstone. So a touchstone being detached does not automaticly represent a bridge being burned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:15:16-07:00","id":119073,"title":"","content":"Indeed, when &quot;bridges get burned&quot; you're losing the touchstone, not detaching it. Detachment merely shows that you care a lot less about the person (from humanity standpoint). It doesn't mean anything changed about the relationship. However it is very likely that it will change, because you no longer care as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:29:03-07:00","id":119077,"title":"","content":"Eh, ok. I have a different interpretation, but you're probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:50:31-07:00","id":119083,"title":"","content":"Your interpretation makes even less sense when you consider that your touchstone does not have to be someone close, someone you interact with directly or even someone at all.<br /> How exactly are you supposed to burn a bridge with your own gravestone ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:52:48-07:00","id":119085,"title":"","content":"Dude, i said you are right, drop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T17:08:34-07:00","id":120042,"title":"","content":"OK, just to sum up:<br /> <br /> 1. Touchstones are lost when they die, are demolished, move without a forwarding address, or otherwise removed from the vampire's personal narrative.<br /> <br /> 2. Touchstones Detached through Humanity loss still exist in said narrative, but no longer have an effect on Detachment rolls.<br /> <br /> 3. Adding a brand new Touchstone to your character's total Touchstone capacity requires a purchase of the so-named Merit.<br /> <br /> 4. Touchstones detached, but not otherwise lost, come back into effect when the vampire's Humanity rises back to the appropriate level.<br /> <br /> 5. Replacing a lost Touchstone, attached or not, requires gaining new Humanity dot, presumably symbolizing the vampire reconnecting with humanity on a psychological level.<br /> <br /> That about cover it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T04:46:11-07:00","id":120289,"title":"","content":"That's it, yes.<br /> <br /> MINOR EDIT: I'll add to 5. that the increase in Humanity is not enough, just necesary. You still need to form a meanigful conection with your Touchstone to be trough roleplaying and interaction. You can't just buy Humanity and then grab the first guy walking down the street and declare him your Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 04-27-2014, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:11:15-07:00","id":586087,"title":"","content":"OK, I know it's been forever, but I have a new question I thought was relevant: If a character still has Touchstones, but they are all Detached, does he still suffer the -2 penalty to detachment rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:26:44-07:00","id":586204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/118911-attachment-of-touchstones?p=586087#post586087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I know it's been forever, but I have a new question I thought was relevant: If a character still has Touchstones, but they are all Detached, does he still suffer the -2 penalty to detachment rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no penalty if you have Detached Touchstones, no matter how many you have. The -2 is only when you have <b>no</b> Touchstones, i.e. when they're all dead/lost/whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}